⚖️ Stream vs Collection in Java
| Feature                | **Collection**                          | **Stream**                                 |
| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| 💾 **Stores data?**    | ✅ Yes (e.g., `List`, `Set`)             | ❌ No (used to **process** data)            |
| 🔄 **Usage**           | Used to **store and retrieve** elements | Used to **process and transform** elements |
| 🔁 **Reusability**     | ✅ Can iterate multiple times            | ❌ One-time use only                        |
| 🧠 **Eager vs Lazy**   | **Eager**: loads everything             | **Lazy**: processes when needed            |
| 🧰 **Operations type** | Structural (add, remove, get)           | Functional (map, filter, reduce)           |
| 🧵 **Parallelism**     | Manual (need threads)                   | ✅ Easy with `parallelStream()`             |
| 🔗 **API Style**       | Imperative                              | Declarative (functional-style)             |
| 🎯 **Modification**    | Can add/remove elements                 | Cannot modify source collection            |
| 📦 **Result**          | Stores objects                          | Returns result or new collection           |


✅ Example: Collection
java
Copy
Edit
List<String> names = new ArrayList<>();
names.add("Ali");
names.add("Ahmed");

for (String name : names) {
    System.out.println(name);
}
✅ Example: Stream
java
Copy
Edit
List<String> names = Arrays.asList("Ali", "Ahmed", "Sara");

names.stream()
    .filter(name -> name.startsWith("A"))
    .map(String::toUpperCase)
    .forEach(System.out::println);  // ALI, AHMED
📌 Use Cases
| Scenario                                      | Use          |
| --------------------------------------------- | ------------ |
| Need to **store and update** data             | `Collection` |
| Need to **process or transform** data         | `Stream`     |
| Want to use **functional programming**        | `Stream`     |
| Working with traditional loops and structures | `Collection` |


✅ Summary Table
| Aspect                      | Collection | Stream                             |
| --------------------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------- |
| Stores data                 | ✅ Yes      | ❌ No                               |
| Supports iteration          | ✅ Yes      | ✅ Yes (but once only)              |
| Supports add/remove         | ✅ Yes      | ❌ No                               |
| Functional methods          | ❌ No       | ✅ Yes                              |
| Lazy evaluation             | ❌ No       | ✅ Yes                              |
| Supports parallel execution | ❌ Manual   | ✅ Built-in with `parallelStream()` |


